
Metro TimeBank System
Copyright 1991 by Peter Deane
-----------------------------


Help
----

Displays this help information.


Quit
----

This never needs explanation.


List Accounts
-------------

Allows you to view a brief listing of
other user accounts. This is good for
obtaining the spelling of a user name
in case you'd like to use the Transfer
Time feature, or simply for the
inquisitive user.


Deposit Time
------------

Allows you to deposit time into your
account for use at a later date. The
Sysop defines how much time a user may
deposit per day. You cannot deposit
more than this limit on any day
(regardless of how many calls or door
entrances you've made).

Also, you may not deposit your full
time remaining balance, you must leave
yourself at least 5 minutes of
remaining time.


Withdraw Time
-------------

Allows you to withdraw time from your
account. The Sysop defines how much
time a user may withdraw per day.
The bank will not let you withdraw more
than this daily limit.

There is no such thing as an overdraft,
either, so you can never leave a
negative balance!


Transfer Time
-------------

Allows you to transfer time from your
account to another user's account. This
time is drawn out of your current
balance, NOT your online time remaining.

The Sysop defines how much time you can
transfer per day.

Any user who has time transferred to
their account will receive a brief
message the next time they enter the
door informing them who transferred the
time, and how much time was transferred.

With ANY transaction, the door will
never allow you to exceed any limit that
may be in force, so you generally will
not have to worry about what the limits
mean.


Reconfigure
-----------

This section will simply allow you to
turn ANSI on or off, and to change your
screen height. You are asked whether you
want ANSI on the door entrance, and your
screen height setting is obtained from
that you have set on the BBS, however
you may like to change either of these
settings while in the door.


Gamble
------

This section will allow you to gamble
with your remaining time (NOT the
account balance). You will have to
withdraw time if you wish to gamble
with more than your remaining time.

Assuming you have enough remaining time
to gamble, the computer will ask how
much you wish to bet. This value must
be an EVEN amount, otherwise the
computer will subtract a dollar from
it, to make it an even amount.

You then bet on a set of two dice
rolls. You'll roll a die, and so will
the house. If your roll is bigger
than or equal to the house's, you win
half your stake.

Then there's a second roll with a
similar outcome.

If you and the house win one round each
there will be no change made to your
remaining time. However: if you lose
both rounds, you'll lose the total of
your bet, or if you win both rounds
you'll win the total of your bet.

Just remember you gamble with your
online time, and NOT your bank balance.

Naturally, if the limits allow, you can
then later deposit or withdraw amounts
depending on how succesful your rolling
has been.

- End Of Text -
